      },
      "text": "The diagnosis should be correlated with the plasma EBV DNA level and radiological staging investigations."
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_negative_correlation",
      "label": "Negative biopsy — clinical correlation",
      "text": "In a patient with a clinically or endoscopically suspicious lesion or a raised plasma EBV DNA level, a negative nasopharyngeal biopsy does not exclude carcinoma; clinical, endoscopic and radiological correlation, with repeat biopsy where indicated, is recommended."
